: HAND-MADE. Typed from Anthropic's documented web search shape, NOT captured from a live account (no search was run: a test never calls a provider).
: Shape per platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/web-search-tool ("Streaming" and "Response"): a text block
: announcing the search, a server_tool_use block streamed like a client tool_use (a start, then an input_json_delta), a
: web_search_tool_result block that arrives COMPLETE in one content_block_start with no deltas (its encrypted_content is the
: string that must come back verbatim), then text blocks, the second carrying a citations_delta (type web_search_result_location,
: with url, title, encrypted_index, cited_text), and usage.server_tool_use.web_search_requests on the final message_delta.
: Per the same page the server_tool_use start carries no input and the id has the srvtoolu_ prefix. The "caller" field on the
: start blocks is copied from the captured tool_use streams (it is "direct" there); the page shows it only for dynamic filtering.
: What this cannot witness: the live wire. The encrypted strings are made up. Replace with a capture at the sitting.

